index 9948571..8681cb5 100644
--- a/base/addons/amxmodx/configs/arp/arp.cfg
+++ b/base/addons/amxmodx/configs/arp/arp.cfg
@@ -77,6 +77,59 @@ arp_welcome_msg1 "This server is running Apollo RP (http://ApolloRP.org)."
 arp_welcome_msg2 "Type 'arp_help' in your console to get started."
 arp_welcome_msg3 "" 
 
+/////////////////////////
+// ARP H9 ADDITIONS
+/////////////////////////
+
+// Every addition H9 made to stock Apollo RP has a switch, and with all of them off (these, and arp_hud_panel, arp_hover_message,
+// arp_hunger_enabled, arp_thirst_enabled, arp_mapsql_autoload) the server plays stock ARP. docs\APOLLO_RP.txt has the table.
+
+// 1: Apollo RP's menus are H9 VGUI panels for the games that draw them, and the inventory and exchange windows are available;
+// 0: every Apollo RP menu is the classic AMX Mod X text menu, whatever the player's game
+arp_h9_vgui "1"
+
+// 1: a dropped item that a player looks toward says what it is and how many (Soda x3), and how to pick it up from close by;
+// 0: stock ARP, which says nothing of it
+arp_h9_itemhover "1"
+
+// The inventory (ARP_Inventory, docs\ARP_INVENTORY.txt): a player's items are arranged in cells, and a game that draws H9 panels has them in a window.
+
+// 1 gives a player whose game has the inventory window that window for /items and /inventory in place of the text menu (it needs arp_h9_vgui 1).
+// 0 gives everybody the text menu. The cell rules below apply to every player either way.
+arp_h9_inv_window "1"
+
+// The cells a player has, 8 to 96 (a grid of 8 columns). A pick-up takes what fits and leaves the rest in the pack, a shop refuses before it takes the
+// money, a give is refused when the other player has no room for all of it, and an add that nothing asked about (a reward, an admin command) falls at
+// the player's feet. Lowering it never takes anything from a player: he keeps his cells until he is back under it.
+// 0 is no limit, as stock ARP: nothing is refused and the grid grows to what is needed.
+arp_h9_inv_slots "32"
+
+// The count of one kind of item in one cell, 1 to 999. configs\arp\inventory.ini names a limit for an item (1: it does not stack).
+arp_h9_inv_stack "20"
+
+// Where a player put his items is kept between his visits: 1 stores the arrangement of his cells in the database (the table arp_h9_cells, made when it is first needed:
+// one row for each character, the cells as text with the item names) and gives it back when he joins, as far as he still owns the items; 0 packs the cells at every join and
+// writes nothing. The counts of the items are ARP's (arp_items) and are never changed by it.
+arp_h9_inv_persist "1"
+
+// A player who presses the use key on a player who is handcuffed or in jail searches him: a window opens with the other player's cells beside his own and what he takes moves
+// from the one's inventory to the other's. 1: on (a game that says _h9vgui 8 draws it, any other gets "That player cannot make an exchange now."); 0: the use key on a handcuffed
+// player does what it did. arp_h9_search_range is how near the searcher must stay once the window is open (units, looked at every second).
+arp_h9_search "1"
+arp_h9_search_range "150"
+
+// What the money is called in the inventory and exchange windows and in the messages ARP_Inventory prints: 1 is credits (1,250 credits), 0 is cash ($1,250).
+// With 1 a player whose game can draw the credit sign (the client that says _h9vgui 7) is also shown the cent sign in place of the "$" of every amount that any Apollo RP
+// plugin prints for him; with 0 every plugin sends what stock ARP sends. The wallet and the bank are ARP's: only the words and the sign change.
+arp_h9_credits "1"
+
+// The exchange of goods between two players (the use key pressed on another player; ARP_Inventory): the distance, in units, at which an open exchange is
+// cancelled. It is looked at every second.
+arp_h9_trade_range "250"
+
+// The seconds without a change to an offer after which an open exchange is cancelled.
+arp_h9_trade_timeout "120"
+
 //////////////
 // ARP CONFIG
 //////////////
